  "_approach": "Cymbal build: the 909 ride goes from alternating 8ths to a rising 16th roll, open hats double into 16ths through the last beat, claps land on the last two offbeats and a pickup kick on the final 16th leads into the drop with the crash. Kick stays 4/4 throughout - the tension comes from the top end. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
